    "readme_description": "The <b>Fibonacci numbers</b>, commonly denoted <code>F(n)</code> form a sequence, called the <b>Fibonacci sequence</b>, such that each number is the sum of the two preceding ones, starting from <code>0</code> and <code>1</code>. That is,\n\n<pre>\nF(0) = 0, F(1) = 1\nF(n) = F(n - 1) + F(n - 2), for n &gt; 1.\n</pre>\n\n<p>Given <code>n</code>, calculate <code>F(n)</code>.</p>",
    "_readme_examples": {
        "list": [
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: n = 2\nOutput: 1\nExplanation: F(2) = F(1) + F(0) = 1 + 0 = 1.\n```"
            },
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: n = 3\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: F(3) = F(2) + F(1) = 1 + 1 = 2.\n```"
            },
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: n = 4\nOutput: 3\nExplanation: F(4) = F(3) + F(2) = 2 + 1 = 3.\n```"
            }
        ]
    },
